      "id": 1,
      "text": "Greenwood was settled in 1824 and officially became a town in 1927.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofgreenwoodfl.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s main street, Fort Road, once ran from a river fort to Pensacola.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofgreenwoodfl.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before the Civil War, Greenwood housed homes like the Hayes House and the Erwin House, some still standing today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofgreenwoodfl.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1930s, a Pure Oil Company service station marked the southern edge of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofgreenwoodfl.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Greenwood’s early economy relied on cotton gins, a peanut mill, and a railroad that operated into the late 1920s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofgreenwoodfl.org/history/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town’s climate features hot, humid summers and mild winters typical of Northwest Florida.",
